From 665da045661747691c8fd230dcbc706181a72e1c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lolipuru <banstellazz@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 04:50:26 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] softisp: Add an edge-aware denoise pass

When the IPA asks for it, the GPU debayer renders into an intermediate
RGBA texture and a second program filters that into the output: a 5x5
bilateral on luma (tight range, keeps edges) and a 5x5 bilateral at a
2-pixel stride on chroma, weighted by luma similarity so colour noise
averages out without bleeding across edges. The filtered luma and chroma
are recombined.

A Denoise IPA algorithm sets the luma and chroma range tolerances from
piecewise-linear tables over analogue gain in the tuning file. Both zero
skips the second pass, so frames in good light take the old single-pass
path. Without the denoise program (shader failure) frames also go
straight to the output.

On the S5K4H7 front camera at 16x gain: luma noise -61%, chroma noise
-77%, 95% of edge strength kept.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: lolipuru <banstellazz@gmail.com>
